From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:48:20 -0400
Subject: give each window a SpaceModel

Spaces belong to a window: the same tab strip is filtered by whichever Space is
active, per ADR 0015. This attaches a SpaceModel to every normal browser window
and gives it an accessor, so the rest of the feature has something to talk to.

The model rides on the window's UnownedUserDataHost, the way UnloadController
does, so SpaceModel::From(browser) works from anywhere that has a
BrowserWindowInterface without threading it through call sites.

Popups and app windows get no SpaceModel. They have a tab strip with nothing to
filter, and From() returning null is the signal to behave exactly as before.

Nothing yet reads this. Tabs still show regardless of Space; that lands with the
filter.

Why: every later piece of Spaces -- the per-tab id, the filter, the switcher,
the window tint -- needs one model per window to hang off.
Removable when: never, short of dropping Spaces.
